DEA-C01 Complete Topic Map
Domain 1: Data Ingestion & Transformation — 34% (~22 questions) 🔥 BIGGEST
This is one-third of your exam. Master this domain or fail.
Task 1.1: Perform Data Ingestion
Streaming ingestion:

Amazon Kinesis family — Streams vs Firehose vs Analytics  Pass IT Exams
Amazon MSK (Managed Kafka)
Amazon Kinesis Data Streams — shards, partition keys, retention, replay
Amazon Data Firehose — buffer config, dynamic partitioning, format conversion
Throttling, exponential backoff, idempotency

Batch ingestion:

AWS DMS (Database Migration Service) — full load, CDC, ongoing replication
AWS DataSync — on-prem to S3/EFS/FSx
AWS Transfer Family — SFTP/FTPS/FTP to S3
AWS Snow Family — Snowball, Snowmobile (large physical transfers)
Amazon AppFlow — SaaS-to-AWS (Salesforce, ServiceNow, Slack)

Task 1.2: Transform & Process Data

AWS Glue — PySpark scripting, job bookmarks, partitioning Pass IT Exams
Glue Spark jobs vs Glue Python Shell vs Glue Ray
AWS Glue DataBrew — visual no-code prep
AWS Lambda — for lightweight transforms
Amazon EMR — Spark, Hive, Presto, Hudi/Iceberg
Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink (KDA Flink) — windowing, joins

Task 1.3: Orchestrate Data Pipelines

AWS Step Functions (Day 4 — your weak area) — state machines, retry, error handling
Amazon EventBridge — schedules, event-driven triggers
Amazon MWAA (Managed Airflow) — DAG-based orchestration
AWS Glue Workflows — for Glue-only pipelines

Task 1.4: Apply Programming Concepts

SQL (joins, window functions, CTEs)
Python basics (Pandas, PySpark)
Infrastructure as Code (CloudFormation, CDK)
Git/CI-CD basics
Data structures (Parquet, ORC, Avro, JSON)


Domain 2: Data Store Management — 26% (~17 questions) 🔥 SECOND BIGGEST
Task 2.1: Choose a Data Store

Amazon S3 — storage classes, lifecycle, intelligent-tiering, S3 Tables (NEW)
Amazon Redshift — RA3 nodes, Serverless, Concurrency Scaling
Amazon DynamoDB — partition keys, GSI/LSI, DAX, on-demand vs provisioned
Amazon RDS / Aurora — when to choose relational
Amazon DocumentDB — MongoDB-compatible
Amazon Neptune — graph database
Amazon Keyspaces — Cassandra-compatible
Amazon OpenSearch — search, log analytics
Amazon MemoryDB / ElastiCache — caching layer

Task 2.2: Design & Manage Data Catalogs

AWS Glue Data Catalog — databases, tables, partitions, classifiers
AWS Glue Crawlers — schedule, schema evolution
AWS Lake Formation — catalog governance

Task 2.3: Manage Data Lifecycle

S3 Lifecycle policies (transition, expiration)
S3 Storage Classes (Standard, IA, One Zone-IA, Glacier Instant/Flexible/Deep Archive)
S3 Intelligent-Tiering
Redshift snapshots, backups
DynamoDB TTL, PITR, on-demand backup
Cross-region replication

Task 2.4: Design Data Models & Schema

Star schema, snowflake schema, fact/dimension tables
Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD Type 1, 2, 3)
Redshift distribution keys (KEY, EVEN, ALL, AUTO)
Redshift sort keys (compound, interleaved)
Partition strategies (S3 Hive-style)
File formats — Parquet, ORC, Avro vs row-based (CSV, JSON)
Compaction, small file problem


Domain 3: Data Operations & Support — 22% (~14 questions)
Task 3.1: Automate Data Processing

AWS Glue Workflows
Step Functions
EventBridge schedules
Lambda triggers
AWS Batch (long-running compute jobs)

Task 3.2: Analyze Data

Amazon Athena — SQL on S3, federated queries, workgroups, query results, partitioning, CTAS
Amazon Redshift Spectrum — query S3 from Redshift
Amazon QuickSight — BI dashboards, SPICE, row-level security
Amazon EMR — Spark/Hive/Presto for big data
AWS Lake Formation governed tables

Task 3.3: Maintain & Monitor Pipelines

Amazon CloudWatch — metrics, logs, alarms
AWS CloudTrail — API audit logs
AWS X-Ray — distributed tracing
Glue job metrics, Spark UI
Redshift system tables (STL, SVL, SVV)
Athena query history

Task 3.4: Ensure Data Quality

AWS Glue Data Quality
AWS Glue DataBrew profile jobs
Deequ (open-source data quality on Spark)
Schema evolution handling
Null checks, uniqueness, completeness, freshness


Domain 4: Data Security & Governance — 18% (~12 questions)
Task 4.1: Authentication

AWS IAM — users, roles, policies, groups
IAM Identity Center (formerly SSO)
IAM federation (SAML, OIDC)
Service-linked roles
Trust policies, AssumeRole, STS

Task 4.2: Authorization

IAM policies (identity-based, resource-based)
S3 bucket policies, ACLs
AWS Lake Formation permissions
Lake Formation tag-based access control (LF-TBAC)
Row-level / column-level / cell-level security
Cross-account access (RAM, resource policies)

Task 4.3: Data Encryption & Masking

AWS KMS — CMK, AWS-managed vs customer-managed keys
SSE-S3, SSE-KMS, SSE-C, DSSE-KMS
Client-side encryption
TLS in transit
Secrets Manager (DB credentials, rotation)
AWS Macie — PII detection
Glue DataBrew PII masking

Task 4.4: Audit Logging

CloudTrail (data events vs management events)
VPC Flow Logs
S3 access logs, S3 server access logging
Redshift audit logs
CloudWatch Logs Insights
AWS Config — compliance monitoring

Task 4.5: Data Privacy & Governance

AWS Lake Formation data filters
Amazon DataZone — data mesh, data catalog
Compliance frameworks (GDPR, HIPAA, PCI-DSS basics)
Data retention policies

